---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import authorImg from '../../content/author/media/author-oleksandr-konovalov-portrait.png';
import PragmaticToolkitModal from '../components/PragmaticToolkitModal.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Oleksandr Konovalov"
  description="Marketing roots, systemic thinking, B2B architecture, and the pre-emptive interview."
>
  <div class="home-canvas">
    <main class="content-column home-main">
      <!-- 0. Brand Logo Mark -->
      <header class="home-brand">
        <a href="/" class="brand-link" aria-label="Oleksandr Konovalov Home">
          <svg class="brand-logo" width="37" height="32" viewBox="0 0 37 32" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M20.5596 0.120946L27.7499 0L31.2404 6.2793L29.1809 9.84149H33.2998L37 15.9998L33.2998 22.1582H29.1806L31.2404 25.7207L27.7499 32L20.5596 31.8791L18.4998 28.3169C18.4998 21.5146 24.0217 16.0002 30.8331 16.0002C24.0218 16.0001 18.5001 10.4858 18.4998 3.68375L20.5596 0.120946ZM3.70016 9.84149H7.81877L5.75962 6.2793L9.25008 0L16.4404 0.120946L18.4998 3.68375C18.4996 10.4859 12.9779 16.0002 6.16662 16.0002C12.9781 16.0002 18.4998 21.5145 18.4998 28.3169L16.4404 31.8791L9.25008 32L5.75962 25.7207L7.81908 22.1582H3.70016L0 15.9998L3.70016 9.84149Z" fill="currentColor"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
      </header>

      <!-- 1. Hero: Author Portrait & Page Title -->
      <section class="about-hero">
        <div class="author-portrait">
          <Image
            src={authorImg}
            alt="Oleksandr Konovalov"
            width={120}
            height={120}
            densities={[1, 2]}
            quality={88}
            class="author-img"
          />
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-display">About me</h1>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Marketing Roots & Systemic Thinking -->
      <section class="block-section">
        <h2 class="text-heading">Marketing Roots & Systemic Thinking</h2>
        <div class="prose-block">
          <p class="text-body-md text-secondary">
            My product design career started in 2017, but my foundation was built in marketing for major automotive brands. That background wired my brain to rely on historical data, potential metrics, and strict processes to manage high-volume workloads.
          </p>
          <p class="text-body-md text-secondary">
            Understanding target audiences directly translated into user-centric design, while my need for structural order led me to adopt Object-Oriented UX (OOUX) via IxDF early in my career. I don't just draw screens; I design for measurable business outcomes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 2. Core Expertise: B2B Architecture & B2C Conversion -->
      <section class="block-section block-section--expertise">
        <h2 class="text-heading">Core Expertise: B2B Architecture & B2C Conversion</h2>
        <ul class="item-list">
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="expertise">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">CRO & Lead Generation</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  The other half of my expertise is Conversion Rate Optimization, shaped by my work at Lemonfrog, Fareportal, and Business Class. I treat CRO like a detective story—relying on heatmaps, traffic sources, and fighting for strict analytics coverage across all interfaces.
                </p>
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  I focus on measurable impact. At Fareportal, iterative design and close collaboration with marketing helped scale the CheapOair Android app revenue from $500k to $3M/month. Recently at Business Class, optimizing the core funnel yielded a +27% conversion lift on mobile (which accounted for &gt;70% of traffic), followed by an additional +12% global lift in the next phase.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="expertise">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">Untangling Complex B2B Systems</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  Currently, I design core internal tools in TravelTech: complex ERPs, B2B platforms, and Salesforce customizations (navigating legacy SLDS constraints). This is where OOUX is critical. TravelTech involves incredibly dense objects and massive state machines interacting across multiple departments. When designing for 400+ internal agents, even a fractional improvement in Error Rate or Task Completeness translates to massive operational ROI.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="expertise">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">Live Prototyping & AI Systems</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  Recently, I’ve shifted to live prototyping. By combining solid OOUX artifacts with an AI-optimized design system, I can build detailed, functional prototypes in minutes, not hours. This drastically accelerates alignment between product stakeholders and engineering.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="expertise">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">Location & Cross-Border Collaboration</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  Based in the Valencia Region, Spain 🇪🇺 for the last 4 years. I am open to relocation within Spain or the broader EU.
                </p>
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  I have extensive experience bridging time zones and working asynchronously. At Fareportal, I collaborated daily with the New York office from Europe, and currently, I manage stakeholders based in Florida. I treat time differences as a process feature, not a bug—utilizing async handoffs and overlapping hours for critical syncs to ensure uninterrupted delivery for US and EU teams.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 3. My Pragmatic Toolkit -->
      <section class="block-section" id="pragmatic-toolkit">
        <h2 class="text-heading">My Pragmatic Toolkit</h2>
        <p class="text-body-md text-secondary">
          Real-world product design is messy. Instead of forcing textbook frameworks like the "Double Diamond," I use a modular toolkit adapted to your actual constraints and legacy code.
        </p>
        <div>
          <a href="#details" class="text-body-1 item-link">See details</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- 4. The Pre-Emptive Interview -->
      <section class="block-section block-section--interview">
        <h2 class="text-heading">The Pre-Emptive Interview</h2>
        <p class="text-body-md text-secondary">
          Let's save us both some calendar space. Here are the direct answers to the operational, technical, and logistical questions design leads ask me most.
        </p>
        <ul class="item-list">
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">How do you handle collaboration across EU and US time zones?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  I structure my day with substantial afternoon/evening overlap with US East and West Coast teams, relying heavily on asynchronous documentation, Loom walkthroughs, and clear ticket handoffs.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">Why do you insist on Object-Oriented UX (OOUX) before wireframing?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  OOUX prevents cognitive overload and UI fragmentation. Mapping objects, relationships, and metadata before drawing screens ensures the design aligns directly with underlying databases and engineering realities.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">You work in both dense B2B systems and B2C conversion. Aren't those conflicting mindsets?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  They complement each other. B2B trains systems architecture, data density, and edge-case resilience, while B2C instills rigorous conversion optimization, speed, and friction reduction.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">How do you approach designing for legacy systems like Salesforce SLDS?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  By respecting existing component constraints and database boundaries first, identifying high-impact UX bottlenecks, and refactoring incrementally rather than proposing unfeasible total rewrites.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">What exactly makes your design systems "AI-adaptive"?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  Semantic token structures, machine-readable specifications, and strict OOUX relationships that LLMs and AI coding agents can parse and execute reliably without hallucinations.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">What is your approach when a project lacks data or clear requirements?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  I map the known business logic, interview frontline stakeholders (support, sales, account managers), and build rapid interactive prototypes to stress-test assumptions and extract concrete feedback.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">What is your work authorization and preferred contract setup?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  Direct B2B contract or international payroll/EOR (Deel, Remote). Fully compliant with EU and international tax and invoicing regulations.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">What team structures are you most comfortable in?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  Cross-functional triads (Product, Design, Engineering) with high autonomy, clear ownership, and direct communication channels.
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
          <li>
            <details class="disclosure-item" name="interview">
              <summary class="disclosure-summary">
                <span class="text-body-1 item-link">What are your working languages?</span>
                <svg class="caret" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M10 12L6 8H14L10 12Z" fill="currentColor"/>
                </svg>
              </summary>
              <div class="disclosure-content disclosure-content--card">
                <p class="text-body-md text-primary">
                  English (fluent, full professional proficiency) and Ukrainian (native).
                </p>
              </div>
            </details>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- 5. Footer -->
      <footer class="home-footer text-body-2 text-disabled">
        <span class="footer-copy">&copy; Lex Konovalov / 2026</span>
        <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Social and contacts">
          <a href="/cv" class="footer-link">CV</a>
          <span class="footer-sep">/</span>
          <a href="mailto:lex.konovalov@gmail.com" class="footer-link">lex.konovalov@gmail.com</a>
          <span class="footer-sep">/</span>
          <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/alexkonovalov" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="footer-link">Linkedin</a>
        </nav>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </div>
  <PragmaticToolkitModal />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ==========================================================================
     Page Canvas & Vertical Rhythm (Identical to Home)
     ========================================================================== */
  .home-canvas {
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding-block: var(--canvas-py-md);
  }

  .home-main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--section-gap-md);
  }

  /* ==========================================================================
     Logo / Brand
     ========================================================================== */
  .home-brand {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .brand-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default);
  }

  .brand-link:hover {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .brand-logo {
    width: 37px;
    height: 32px;
  }

  /* ==========================================================================
     About Hero: Portrait & Title
     ========================================================================== */
  .about-hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-16);
  }

  .author-portrait {
    width: var(--author-photo-size);
    height: var(--author-photo-size);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .author-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    display: block;
  }

  /* ==========================================================================
     Block Sections & Prose
     ========================================================================== */
  .block-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--container-gap-sm);
  }

  .prose-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  /* ==========================================================================
     Color Tone Utility Application
     ========================================================================== */
  .text-primary {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }

  .text-secondary {
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .text-disabled {
    color: var(--color-text-disabled);
  }

  /* ==========================================================================
     Lists, Links & Disclosures
     ========================================================================== */
  .item-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--container-gap-sm);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .item-link {
    display: inline-block;
    color: var(--color-text-link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    width: fit-content;
    transition: opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default);
  }

  .item-link:hover {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .disclosure-item {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .disclosure-summary {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    list-style: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    user-select: none;
    width: fit-content;
  }

  .disclosure-summary::-webkit-details-marker,
  .disclosure-summary::marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .disclosure-summary:hover .item-link,
  .disclosure-summary:hover .caret {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .disclosure-summary .caret {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    color: var(--color-text-link);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    transition: transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default), opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default);
  }

  .disclosure-item[open] .caret {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }

  .disclosure-item[open] > .disclosure-summary .item-link {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .block-section--expertise,
  .block-section--interview {
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .block-section--expertise .item-list,
  .block-section--interview .item-list {
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .disclosure-content {
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    padding-left: var(--space-1);
  }

  .disclosure-content--card {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding: var(--space-6);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--color-surface-subtle);
  }

  /* ==========================================================================
     Footer
     ========================================================================== */
  .home-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .footer-copy {
    color: var(--color-text-disabled);
  }

  .footer-nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
  }

  .footer-link {
    color: var(--color-text-link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    transition: opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default);
  }

  .footer-link:hover,
  .footer-link:focus-visible {
    opacity: 0.75;
  }

  .footer-sep {
    color: var(--color-text-disabled);
    user-select: none;
  }

  /* Mobile adjustment for footer */
  @media (max-width: 500px) {
    .home-footer {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: var(--space-2);
    }
  }
</style>
